# The sentinel that runs .github/workflows/ledger-imagegen.yml.
#
# Touching this file and pushing generates Meridian signage on Jafar's PC, on
# the self-hosted runner labelled `ledger-pc` that four other workflows already
# use. It needs no click from him and no account: the model is Apache-2.0 and
# nothing here is purchased. The point of the lane is that this compute is
# FREE against the weekly Claude ceiling and runs while nobody is working.
#
# It exists because a workflow_dispatch workflow must live on the default
# branch to be dispatchable, and this one lives on the working branch by
# standing instruction. Delete this file and the push trigger together when
# the workflow reaches main; the dispatch entry there is already correct and
# takes limit / only / max_minutes as inputs.
#
# It sits HERE, beside DISPATCH, SETUP-MSVC, SETUP-BLENDER and FETCH-VIGNETTE,
# and NOT in ledger/Assets/StreamingAssets/Decals/generated, because that
# directory is the job's OUTPUT and a trigger inside an output directory is how
# a run re-fires itself.
#
# WHAT A SENTINEL PUSH GENERATES, and how to change it. The push path cannot
# carry dispatch inputs, so the batch is whatever the workflow's BATCH_LIMIT,
# BATCH_ONLY and BATCH_MAX_MINUTES fall back to: 4 pictures, chosen by
# prompts.json order, 60 minutes of loop. `--limit` bounds what a run
# GENERATES rather than where it starts, so items already on disk are skipped
# for free and each dispatch takes the next four. To run a different batch,
# edit those three fallbacks in the workflow in the same commit that touches
# this file.
#
# WHAT THE FIRST RUN IS FOR. Proving the route, not filling the queue. 31 of
# the 45 written prompts have never been generated, and a night that produces
# 31 blank PNGs plus a manifest describing them as art is worse than a night
# with no run at all (leejet/stable-diffusion.cpp#1031: Z-Image on Vulkan can
# write a blank PNG and exit zero). So the first dispatch makes four, the run
# stops at the first blank, and the verdict re-measures every PNG from its own
# pixels before anything is called banked.
#
# One line per run, appended, so this file is also the dispatch log.
#
# run 1 - UNRUN as this file is written. Expected: sign_ferry,
# sign_harbour_master, sign_weighbridge and sign_telephone, the first four
# items of tools/imagegen/prompts.json with no PNG on disk, 768x512 each, an
# estimated 68 seconds each on the card measured 25 Aug. The verdict lands at
# ledger/Assets/StreamingAssets/Decals/generated/imagegen-verdict.txt with the
# commit on line 1.
#
# run 1 - RAN 2026-09-02 on b8b805f2 (run 33654488608), 105 s, FAILED at the
# setup step `The commit this run is measuring` in 0 s; all four work steps
# skipped; nothing banked, nothing carried forward. Cause: git ran in that
# step without the safe.directory env every other git step on ledger-pc
# carries, and the commit step's own git rev-parse succeeded under it in the
# same run. A second fault: the verdict was printed and staged=0. Ruling:
# game-design/decision-2026-09-02-imagegen-run1-stopper-and-run2.md.
#
# run 2 - fired by the push that lands that ruling. Same four items expected.
# The verdict's steps line now carries stopper= and shaFrom=, and the commit
# step prints every staging candidate with %q, so a trailing \r from Windows
# Python shows as $'\r' and the second fault is measured, not believed.
